--TEST--
`Core\BigInt::format` and `parse` round-trip through all 35 radixes, and text that is not an integer in the radix asked for is a `ParseError` while a radix outside 2 to 36 is a `LogicError` — `rule:core-api/shape-rules` and `rule:types/conversion`, spec § 13
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `format` writes and `parse` reads back, so a round trip through *every*
// radix is one property asserted 35 times. Counting it is what catches a base
// whose digit class is wrong in one direction only — a member that wrote `z`
// and read `Z` prints correctly at 10 and 16 and fails here.
var $value = Core\BigInt::parse("-123456789012345678901234567890");
uint $radix = 2;
int $round = 0;
while ($radix <= 36) {
    var $written = $value->format({radix: $radix});
    if (Core\BigInt::parse($written, {radix: $radix})->compareTo($value) == 0) {
        $round = $round + 1;
    }
    $radix = $radix + 1;
}
echo "round trips ", $round, " of 35\n";
echo "b36 ", $value->format({radix: 36}), "\n";
echo "b2 ", Core\BigInt::of(-10)->format({radix: 2}), " b8 ", Core\BigInt::of(-10)->format({radix: 8}), " b10 ", Core\BigInt::of(-10)->toString(), "\n";

// The boundary a radix *is*: `1a` is a number from 11 up and not below it, so
// one text swept across the range names the first radix that has the digit.
int $accepted = 0;
uint $first = 0;
$radix = 2;
while ($radix <= 36) {
    try {
        Core\BigInt::parse("1a", {radix: $radix});
        $accepted = $accepted + 1;
        if ($first == 0) {
            $first = $radix;
        }
    } catch (ParseError $noDigit) {
        $accepted = $accepted + 0;
    }
    $radix = $radix + 1;
}
echo "1a parsed in ", $accepted, " radixes, first ", $first, "\n";

// What is not an integer in any radix: the whole text is read, so a separator,
// a point, a space and a base prefix are each a refusal rather than a prefix
// that stopped early. `1_000` is refused for the reason `"1_000" as int`
// refuses it — the separator is an integer *literal*'s spelling.
array<string> $bad = ["", "12.5", " 7", "1_000", "0x1f", "-"];
int $refusals = 0;
string $firstRefusal = "";
foreach ($bad as string $text) {
    try {
        Core\BigInt::parse($text);
    } catch (ParseError $notAnInteger) {
        $refusals = $refusals + 1;
        if ($refusals == 1) {
            $firstRefusal = $notAnInteger->message;
        }
    }
}
echo "refused ", $refusals, " of 6: ", $firstRefusal, "\n";

// A radix outside the range is the program's bug rather than its input's, so
// it is the other class — and both members carrying the bag answer alike.
try {
    Core\BigInt::parse("10", {radix: 1});
} catch (LogicError $tooNarrow) {
    echo "parse: ", $tooNarrow->message, "\n";
}
try {
    Core\BigInt::ofUint(255)->format({radix: 37});
} catch (LogicError $tooWide) {
    echo "format: ", $tooWide->message, "\n";
}
--EXPECT--
round trips 35 of 35
b36 -byw97um9s91dlz68tsi
b2 -1010 b8 -12 b10 -10
1a parsed in 26 radixes, first 11
refused 6 of 6: Core\BigInt::parse(): `` is not an integer in radix 10
parse: Core\BigInt::parse(): radix 1 is outside the 2 to 36 this class reads and writes
format: Core\BigInt::format(): radix 37 is outside the 2 to 36 this class reads and writes
